3.2 Technical Components
Component 1: Data Acquisition & Preprocessing

Source: Amazon Customer Reviews Dataset (UCSD - 233M reviews, free)
Subset: 50,000 reviews (Electronics category)
Cleaning: Remove duplicates, non-English, <20 character reviews
Labeling: Semi-supervised approach for return intent (keyword-based + manual validation)

Component 2: Feature Engineering

Text Features: TF-IDF (5,000 vocab), BERT embeddings (768-dim), sentiment lexicons (VADER)
Linguistic Features: Temporal patterns, negation handling, sarcasm indicators
Metadata Features: Verified purchase, review length, helpfulness ratio, rating-text consistency
Contextual Features: Product category, price tier, brand, review age

Component 3: Machine Learning Models
Model 1: Aspect Extraction

Architecture: BERT-base fine-tuned for multi-label classification
Input: Review text (512 tokens max)
Output: Binary labels for 8 aspects [battery, screen, price, quality, design, shipping, service, durability]
Training: Binary cross-entropy loss, 3 epochs, learning rate 2e-5
Performance Target: F1 > 0.80

Model 2: Aspect Sentiment Classification

Architecture: Logistic Regression (per aspect) on sentence embeddings
Input: Aspect-relevant sentences extracted via cosine similarity
Output: Positive/Negative/Neutral per aspect
Features: VADER polarity, TF-IDF, negation flags
Performance Target: Accuracy > 0.85

Model 3: Return Intent Prediction

Architecture: XGBoost Classifier
Input: BERT embeddings + engineered features (temporal flags, rating mismatch, failure keywords)
Output: Probability of return (0-1)
Class Balancing: SMOTE oversampling + class weights (3:1)
Performance Target: F1 > 0.75, Precision > 0.80

Model 4: Review Authenticity Detection

Architecture: Isolation Forest (anomaly detection) + Logistic Regression
Input: Linguistic features (generic language score), metadata (verified purchase, review timing)
Output: Authenticity score (0-100%)
Performance Target: Precision > 0.85 (minimize false accusations)

Component 4: Interactive Dashboard (Streamlit)

Input Interface: CSV upload or Amazon URL paste
Visualizations: Aspect sentiment bars, return risk table, trend charts
Interactivity: Click reviews to see details, sort by risk score, filter by aspect
Export: Download insights as CSV/PDF reports

